            <div type="translation" xml:lang="en" resp="#AA">
                <p>To Gaius Memmius Marianus, son of Gaius, of tribe Aniensus, flamen of the divine Claudius, duovir, triumvir, curator of temple, quaestor of the food fund, the residents of the Velabrum district to their patron, on account of his merits.
                   At the dedication of this monument, he gave eight sesterces to each individual. This place was given by decree the decurions.
                </p>
